 },
 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Removing a regular point to arrange infinity",
 "statement": "Let $\\mathcal F$ be a punctually pure lisse Weil sheaf of weight $w$\non a dense open $U_0\\subset\\mathbf A^1_{k_0}$.\nAfter a finite constant-field extension, there are a dense open\n$V_0\\subset\\mathbf A^1$ and a lisse sheaf $\\mathcal E$ on $V_0$\nof the same weight, with trivial local inertia at infinity, together\nwith a Frobenius-equivariant surjection\n\n$$\nH_c^1(V,\\mathcal E)\\twoheadrightarrow H_c^1(U,\\mathcal F).\n$$\n\nGeometric irreducibility is preserved.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-deligne-laumon-a1/sk-thm-dl-a1-upper/lem-a1-unramified-at-infinity.md",
  "place": "node lem-a1-unramified-at-infinity, order 2800"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "def-weil-pbc-scheme-conventions",
  "def-wf-middle-extension"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "Choose a geometric point $s\\in U$, defined over a finite extension.\nOver a further finite extension choose\n$\\tau\\in\\mathrm{PGL}_2$ with $\\tau(s)=\\infty$.\nSet $V_0=\\tau(U_0\\setminus\\{s\\})\\subset\\mathbf A^1$ and let\n$\\mathcal E$ be the transported restriction.\nIt extends lisse across infinity, since $\\mathcal F$ was lisse at\n$s$; hence its inertia there is trivial.\nRestriction to a dense open preserves geometric irreducibility:\nthe fundamental group of that open surjects onto the fundamental\ngroup of the original smooth curve, by\n[lem-wf-dense-open-pi1-surjective] (parts (1) and (4)).\nThe isomorphism $\\tau$ and restriction preserve the local\nweight condition of [def-weil-punctual-weights].",
   "uses": [
    "lem-wf-dense-open-pi1-surjective",
    "def-weil-punctual-weights"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  },
  {
   "text": "Open–closed recollement, [def-weil-open-closed-recollement], whose triangle exists for\n$\\Qlb$-Weil sheaves by [prop-sf-open-closed-triangle-all-stages],\nand the vanishing of $H_c^1$ on the single point from\n[lem-a1-finite-boundary-cohomology] give a surjection\n$H_c^1(U\\setminus\\{s\\},\\mathcal F)\\to H_c^1(U,\\mathcal F)$.\nTransport by $\\tau$ gives the asserted map in the convention of\n[def-weil-ordinary-compact-cohomology].",
   "uses": [
    "def-weil-open-closed-recollement",
    "prop-sf-open-closed-triangle-all-stages",
    "lem-a1-finite-boundary-cohomology",
    "def-weil-ordinary-compact-cohomology"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
